### Environment API

Import from `@talex-touch/tuffex`.

| Export | Signature | When to use |
|--------|-----------|-------------|
| `notifySurfaceWindowMotion()` | `() => void` | Call it as the host forwards window moves; the window counts as still once 140ms pass without a call. |
| `setSurfacePowerSaving(value)` | `(value: boolean \| null) => void` | Overrides the power-saving reading from the host; `null` hands it back to the Battery Status API (not charging, at or below 20%). |
| `getSurfaceEnvironment()` | `() => { pointerMoving, windowMoving, powerSaving, frameTier }` | Reads the page's current environment as read-only refs; `frameTier` is `'ok' \| 'reduced' \| 'minimal'`. |
| `useSurfaceMotionGuard(emitFallback, options?)` | `(emitFallback: (isFallback: boolean) => void, { settleMs? }) => { onMotionStart, onMotionEnd, dispose }` | For hosts that know when they move: drives `moving` with the asymmetric clock, calling back `true` at once on start and `false` after `settleMs` (140ms by default) of quiet. |
| `SURFACE_POINTER_SPEED_THRESHOLD` / `SURFACE_MOTION_SETTLE_MS` / `SURFACE_LOW_BATTERY_LEVEL` | `1.2` / `140` / `0.2` | The pointer speed threshold (px/ms), how long a motion signal stays quiet before it ends (ms), and the low-battery level. |

## Overview

- `pure` and `flat` render only the root background; `mask` renders a mask layer with opacity clamped to `0..1`; `acrylic` is a filter layer blurring three times as wide under a tint whose alpha carries fractal noise; `mica` paints the root with an opaque base and two glows anchored to the viewport (`background-attachment: fixed`), reading no backdrop but repainting with every scroll of its container, so keep it off bases that scroll; `plain` keeps only the radius and the overflow clip.
- `blur`, `glass` and `acrylic` degrade while `moving` is set or `autoDetect` senses motion: `fallbackMode="mask"` prefers `fallbackMaskOpacity`, and `pure` and `flat` render no mask layer.
- `refraction` keeps its mode in motion: the glass / blur layers that lose their sampling fade out, a translucent motion cover holds the weight, and both cross-fade back on settle.
- Passing any of `refractionStrength`, `refractionAngle`, or `refractionProfile` switches to the derived refraction model; unset ones fall back to `62` / `-24` / `'filmic'`.
- `autoDetect` listens on the root and every ancestor for their own `transform` / `translate` transitions (`transitionstart` / `transitionend` / `transitioncancel`) and watches their inline `style` with a `MutationObserver`; the pointer, window, frame-probe and battery listeners are page-wide, shared by every surface with `autoDetect`, and removed when the last one unmounts.
- With `systemBackdrop`, the glass layer doesn't render and the filter layer's `backdrop-filter` is `none`, keeping its tint; neither the motion fallback nor environment sensing runs. The veil, mask, flow light and rim are unaffected.
- Under high contrast (triggers in [Theming](./theming.en.mdc)), every mode but `plain` paints only the opaque root background, like `pure`: the glass, blur, mask, motion-cover and refraction-edge layers don't render, and the `fake` base shows at full opacity; `plain` gets no fill even then.

## Technologies

- Glass and refraction render through `TxGlassSurface`; fallback timing lives in `base-surface-motion.ts`, and the page-wide environment sensing and material degradation in `surface-environment.ts`.
